{"name":"Just be famous theory","deep":true,"image":null,"mentions":66,"casual":{"lead":["Just be famous (JBF) is a framework discussed on looksmaxxing forums. It argues that a man with average or below-average looks can still gain romantic and social success if he becomes famous, because celebrity brings attention and status that overshadow facial ratings.","It is usually raised in debates about how much looks matter, often with examples of publicly known couples where the man is rated lower on the community's scales. A looksmax.org thread uses the phrase in its title alongside a rating on the PSL scale and a supermodel partner."],"sections":[{"h":"How people use it","paras":["In practice the theory is a way of thinking rather than a routine: proponents point to building an audience, career or visibility as the lever instead of or alongside surgery and grooming."],"subs":[]},{"h":"Risks & side effects","paras":["The framework carries no physical risk. Critics inside and outside forums note that fame is rare and that attractiveness research shows halo effects in both directions."],"subs":[]}]},"gallery":[],"links":{"studies":[{"title":"Optimally estimating the sample mean from the sample size, median, mid-range, and/or mid-quartile range.","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/27683581/","source":"Statistical methods in medical research","year":2018,"cites":3062,"kind":null},{"title":"Memory, navigation and theta rhythm in the hippocampal-entorhinal system.","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/23354386/","source":"Nature neuroscience","year":2013,"cites":1494,"kind":"Review"},{"title":"Mediterranean diet pyramid: a cultural model for healthy eating.","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/7754995/","source":"The American journal of clinical nutrition","year":1995,"cites":1460,"kind":"Review"},{"title":"Object-related activity revealed by functional magnetic resonance imaging in human occipital cortex.","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/7667258/","source":"P